This repository is under two licences, because it holds two different kinds of
thing.

The content — the prose, the diagrams, the element and test data, everything a
reader sees on the site — is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0). See
LICENSE-CONTENT.

The code — the build, the derivation in src/lib/, the drawing and checking tools
in tools/, the components and layouts — is licensed under the MIT licence, set
out in full below.

Where the two meet, the test is what the file is for: the words and figures a
reader sees are content wherever they happen to live in the tree, and the
machinery that produces them is code.

The governing-body syllabus documents in sources/ are not in this repository and
are not covered by either licence. They are read locally and never redistributed.

